WEBVTT

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.310
Chloe, the book of Rao isn't here.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.810
I know you just came across that footage,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.810
but there's got to be something more on it.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:15.810
I'm looking at it now, Clark.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.809
Jarrell, put it in the North Wall.

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:18.809
I wish I could give you more.

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:20.809
But thanks to Tess' little break-in,

00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:22.809
Watchtower can barely run a game of Donkey Kong,

00:00:22.809 --> 00:00:24.809
let alone an image enhancement program.

00:00:24.809 --> 00:00:27.809
Chloe, if that book really holds unlimited power,

00:00:27.809 --> 00:00:28.809
then we need to find it.

00:00:28.809 --> 00:00:31.809
You know, Clark, this could explain why our favorite alien nation

00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:32.810
has gone awall.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.810
I mean, maybe Zod and the Kandorians are trying

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.810
to track down the Holy Rao Grail before we do.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:52.020
We gotta go.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.020
Mullis.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.299
Mark.

00:00:55.299 --> 00:00:56.299
I'm sorry, I thought you were a...

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:59.289
Thief?

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:01.289
If you can't recognize my butt in a pair of jeans,

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:02.289
then what are you thinking about?

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:03.289
I know.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:04.290
I just, I've been distracted.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.290
Well, excuse me for getting between a man and his tractor,

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:09.290
but our unemployment situation has just gone to DefCon 1.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.290
Paulus, it's not a matter of life and death.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.290
Actually, it is.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:17.290
My phone just got turned off because the planet stopped paying my cell bill

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:20.290
and half my wardrobe is being held hostage at the dry cleaners.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.290
To top it off, it's as if you're expecting me

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.290
to single-handedly save our unemployed deriers.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:28.290
Floyd Derriers, which lucky for you, I have.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.290
I have found a story that will get us corner offices at the planet

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.290
with parking on P1. We just have to start now.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.290
Look, I appreciate the offer lowest, but I can't drop everything right now.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:41.730
Whoa! Hey, I have been pounding back double-double espresso.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:46.730
Just trying to keep us on some kind of a masthead, and you've been doing what exactly?

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:50.730
I just have some responsibilities that I can't ignore.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.730
Well, here's something I can't ignore. I need a purpose.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:57.730
Some kind of bigger mission in life.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.730
You don't seem to need that.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.730
Lois, you're under a lot of stress right now.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.730
I understand that, but maybe you're just overreacting.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:10.080
To what?

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.520
My life falling apart?

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.520
Lois, just give me a break.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.520
You want a break.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:25.349
Maybe we should take a break.

00:02:25.349 --> 00:02:26.349
A break from this relationship.

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:36.379
Clark!

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:39.659
Mom? What a surprise.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.659
I thought you'd be at the planet.

00:02:41.659 --> 00:02:46.219
I'm working from home.

00:02:46.219 --> 00:02:47.219
What do you?

00:02:47.219 --> 00:02:48.219
What are you doing here?

00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:50.219
I need an excuse to see my own son.

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:51.219
Louis, hi.

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:53.219
You'll stay for dinner, I hope.

00:02:53.219 --> 00:02:57.860
I've got plenty for the four of us.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.300
The four of us?

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.860
I don't know why you need all these clothes.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.860
My help, you won't be wearing any.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:11.069
You remember Perry White?

00:03:11.069 --> 00:04:32.560
The Perry White?

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.889
I think about him every day.

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:41.889
Your father and I had our first date in this barn.

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:45.889
I'd made a surprise picnic, but his truck broke down, so...

00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:47.889
We ate it in here.

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:50.889
I'm glad you made it home, Mom.

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:52.889
Well, the Senate broke early for recess,

00:04:52.889 --> 00:05:03.040
and the truth is, I couldn't face the memories.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.040
It's hard coming back to this place.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:17.649
I'm just glad you're here now.

00:05:17.649 --> 00:05:18.649
About Perry.

00:05:18.649 --> 00:05:20.649
I hope you don't mind.

00:05:20.649 --> 00:05:24.649
I bumped into him at a committee hearing a few months ago.

00:05:24.649 --> 00:05:28.089
It's okay, Mom.

00:05:28.089 --> 00:05:30.089
As long as he doesn't start looking for a story,

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:31.089
that may have a story.

00:05:31.089 --> 00:05:33.089
hands full with the Chandorians.

00:05:33.089 --> 00:05:36.089
I'm so proud of everything you're doing to help your people.

00:05:36.089 --> 00:05:38.089
It hasn't been easy.

00:05:38.089 --> 00:05:41.089
More than ever, I've been living two lives.

00:05:41.089 --> 00:05:44.089
One of those lives is full of sacrifice,

00:05:44.089 --> 00:05:47.089
so I'm glad to see the other one has Lois in it.

00:05:47.089 --> 00:05:51.089
I sleep better knowing you have someone special in your life.

00:05:51.089 --> 00:06:01.350
Oh my God, you've got to forward this to my high school journalism teacher.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.350
Check it out, Mrs. Kreidzman, me and Perry White.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:06.350
Who's sorry now, Björch?

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:07.350
Sorry, kid.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.329
The last thing I need is a Mrs.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.350
Kreitzmann on my ass.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.350
By the way, I've read some of your stuff.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.350
You and Clark are a regular Woodward and Bernstein.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.350
Thanks.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.350
We aren't really writing together at the moment.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.350
Is that you next big story?

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.350
Yeah, I've been tracking this one for months.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.350
Big players.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.350
This thing is my white whale, kid.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.350
Sorry, I can't share any details.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.350
Too bad, Ahab.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.350
Because I've got something pretty big on the line, too.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.350
It's going to cause quite a splash.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:42.350
Oh, well, if it's as huge as you say it is,

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.350
good luck reeling it in all by yourself.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:48.759
That's true.

00:06:48.759 --> 00:06:51.759
I don't have Clark right now to help with the heavy lifting.

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:56.579
But this puppy sells itself.

00:06:56.579 --> 00:07:00.579
It is going to kick your story back to arts and leisure.

00:07:00.579 --> 00:07:09.079
You've got to be kidding me.

00:07:09.079 --> 00:07:12.079
This is a goff guy on a trampoline in a jogging suit.

00:07:12.079 --> 00:07:14.079
No, it's the real thing.

00:07:14.079 --> 00:07:16.079
I got a call from a...

00:07:16.079 --> 00:07:18.740
A guy who needs to be a...

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.740
He did my help.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.740
And when I started investigating this shady redhead,

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.740
I found the mother load.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.740
There are aliens here on our planet.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:33.660
And they are looking for this.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:37.139
The Book of Rao.

00:07:37.139 --> 00:07:39.139
The Book of Rao.

00:07:39.139 --> 00:07:43.139
Really? I've seen this before.

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:47.279
You gotta give some to get some.

00:07:47.279 --> 00:07:53.889
All right, Lane.

00:07:53.889 --> 00:07:54.889
Here's what I've got.

00:07:54.889 --> 00:07:58.889
A secret government complex in the Rocky Mountains was blown to bits.

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:03.889
trying to investigate. I was blocked by an operative even the FBI doesn't know about it.

00:08:03.889 --> 00:08:05.889
The code name Red Queen.

00:08:05.889 --> 00:08:09.889
Yeah, I think she's shadowing a secret organization called Checkmate,

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.889
which is fighting some kind of terrorist invasion.

00:08:12.889 --> 00:08:16.889
And it's all somehow connected with this.

00:08:16.889 --> 00:08:21.889
Maybe our two stories are really the same story.

00:08:21.889 --> 00:08:24.889
This is your lucky day, kid.

00:08:24.889 --> 00:08:27.889
The big break most people only dream about.

00:08:27.889 --> 00:08:31.889
You get to write a story with Perry White.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:45.789
It's the book of Rao.

00:09:45.789 --> 00:09:46.789
Got to hand it to you, Mrs. K.

00:09:46.789 --> 00:09:50.789
Running Senate subcommittees by day, cooking and rocking meals by night.

00:09:50.789 --> 00:09:52.789
You put the Amin Modern Woman.

00:09:52.789 --> 00:09:54.789
Me, I put the tea in takeout.

00:09:54.789 --> 00:09:57.789
So, tell me all the news.

00:09:57.789 --> 00:09:59.789
How are you in Clark?

00:09:59.789 --> 00:10:03.789
Oh, you know, everything's peachy.

00:10:03.789 --> 00:10:04.789
You know us?

00:10:04.789 --> 00:10:10.200
Chocolate and peanut butter, Yan and Yang, Tarzan and Jane.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.200
Okay, maybe not the pie.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.580
holding hair, jungle, love of it all.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.580
Perry mentioned you aren't writing together.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.580
Is everything okay?

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.580
Yeah.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:24.590
Have you ever wanted to do something really important with your life?

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:29.759
Right.

00:10:29.759 --> 00:10:32.759
The senator thing kind of says it all.

00:10:32.759 --> 00:10:38.139
It wasn't easy for me to leave Clark and go to Washington.

00:10:38.139 --> 00:10:43.139
But a part of me really needed to take that next step.

00:10:43.139 --> 00:10:46.139
That is exactly how I felt when I was talking to...

00:10:46.139 --> 00:10:55.179
This friend, we used to work together.

00:10:55.179 --> 00:10:56.179
We used to work together.

00:10:56.179 --> 00:11:03.580
And when I helped him, it was like I had a higher purpose.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:08.950
Like I was saving the world.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:15.929
You know, after the glow of my wedding wore off,

00:11:15.929 --> 00:11:18.929
I wondered if I'd made a huge mistake,

00:11:18.929 --> 00:11:21.929
following Jonathan to a small town where I didn't fit in.

00:11:21.929 --> 00:11:24.929
I went from a city social I'd headed for law school

00:11:24.929 --> 00:11:29.929
to being a farmer's wife marooned on an island of corn.

00:11:29.929 --> 00:11:31.929
Sounds like survivors.

00:11:31.929 --> 00:11:33.929
small milk.

00:11:33.929 --> 00:11:38.929
You can imagine how I felt when I was offered a job interning for a federal judge.

00:11:38.929 --> 00:11:40.929
I just jumped at the chance.

00:11:40.929 --> 00:11:43.929
It was such an exciting time of my life.

00:11:43.929 --> 00:11:49.230
But in the end, you didn't stay.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:56.669
I came home on a rainy weekend and discovered the river was rising.

00:11:56.669 --> 00:12:02.669
So I pulled on workboots and went down to the river with Jonathan.

00:12:02.669 --> 00:12:04.669
We started throwing sandbags.

00:12:04.669 --> 00:12:05.669
We worked all around.

00:12:05.669 --> 00:12:08.669
all night, holding back a wall of water.

00:12:08.669 --> 00:12:16.840
When the sun rose, I got to tell 20 families

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.840
that it was safe to go home again.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:23.789
The city girl saves the day.

00:12:23.789 --> 00:12:27.789
I didn't know what my purpose really was until that rainy day.

00:12:27.789 --> 00:12:32.360
I needed to look inside myself.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:42.909
Listen, Clark, the Candorians are still MIA.

00:12:42.909 --> 00:12:43.909
What about the Book of Row?

00:12:43.909 --> 00:12:45.909
I've searched the entire farm. It's not here.

00:12:45.909 --> 00:12:47.909
Yeah, well, lucky for us.

00:12:47.909 --> 00:12:49.909
My mini watchtower that could is actually pulling all

00:12:49.909 --> 00:12:52.909
and monster wide web search.

00:12:52.909 --> 00:12:55.909
So if there's any mention of the Book of Row anywhere in this...

00:12:55.909 --> 00:13:03.919
News, Clark.

00:13:03.919 --> 00:13:06.919
It looks like I just got a Red Queen virtual Smackdown.

00:13:06.919 --> 00:13:08.919
Red Queen.

00:13:08.919 --> 00:13:10.919
Chloe, that sounds like Checkmate.

00:13:10.919 --> 00:13:12.919
Yeah, well, despite her handle, the Red Queen isn't actually

00:13:12.919 --> 00:13:14.919
a figure on Checkmate's board.

00:13:14.919 --> 00:13:16.919
In fact, the rumor has it, that her name has been filed

00:13:16.919 --> 00:13:18.919
under Big Bad Nemesis.

00:13:18.919 --> 00:13:22.870
I'll be there as soon as I can.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:31.419
I'm sort of held hostage here until after my mom's family dinner.

00:13:31.419 --> 00:13:32.419
That's it, join me in a drink.

00:13:32.419 --> 00:13:38.669
Club soda.

00:13:38.669 --> 00:13:41.669
Since that little wake-up call of yours years ago,

00:13:41.669 --> 00:13:43.669
I'm a teetotaler, and an utter boar.

00:13:43.669 --> 00:13:49.100
Still chasing down stories, I see.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:53.100
Oh, this is a little freelance project I'm doing on the side.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.100
With Lois, actually.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.789
I hope I'm not overstepping.

00:13:58.789 --> 00:14:00.789
Oh.

00:14:00.789 --> 00:14:04.789
There was this one story she wanted my help on, but...

00:14:04.789 --> 00:14:07.789
Looks like she's traded up for a more...

00:14:07.789 --> 00:14:09.789
...experienced partner.

00:14:09.789 --> 00:14:12.419
Let you know a little secret.

00:14:12.419 --> 00:14:15.419
A little secret. Experience is overrated.

00:14:15.419 --> 00:14:19.820
I spent the first 20 years of my career

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:22.820
living out of a carry-on bag, chasing every story that moved.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.820
I was saving the world.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:27.820
It's a big job for a simple reporter.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:30.820
Yeah, well, two ex-wives and an ex-dog later.

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:32.820
It finally sunk in.

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.820
What matters most is having someone around to share your life with.

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:45.759
Someone like your mom.

00:14:45.759 --> 00:14:46.759
Clark.

00:14:46.759 --> 00:14:48.759
Here's the thing.

00:14:48.759 --> 00:14:50.759
I'm going to ask your mother to marry me.

00:14:50.759 --> 00:14:55.980
I'd like your blessing.

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:56.980
Your blessing.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:08.690
Listen, Mr. White, I don't want to get in the middle of anything.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:22.309
I'm not sure she's going to give you the answer you're looking for.

00:15:22.309 --> 00:15:24.309
Lois, we need a talk.

00:15:24.309 --> 00:15:26.309
I don't want to take a break.

00:15:26.309 --> 00:15:28.309
I still believe in us.

00:15:28.309 --> 00:15:30.309
I want to believe in us, too.

00:15:30.309 --> 00:15:33.309
There's a lot I have to figure out, and I can't keep lying to everyone about us.

00:15:33.309 --> 00:15:35.309
Mom, everything smells great.

00:15:35.309 --> 00:15:37.309
Thanks, honey.

00:15:37.309 --> 00:15:54.320
Could you two help me with the...

00:15:54.320 --> 00:16:01.919
Who's up for a crackling fire?

00:16:01.919 --> 00:16:04.490
What did I do?

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:30.389
That was my dad's jacket.

00:16:30.389 --> 00:16:31.389
What a spread.

00:16:31.389 --> 00:16:35.639
Really outdid yourself, honey.

00:16:35.639 --> 00:16:41.899
All right, you love birds.

00:16:41.899 --> 00:16:44.899
Tell us what it's like working together and dating.

00:16:44.899 --> 00:16:47.899
It's never been better?

00:16:47.899 --> 00:16:52.779
It's kind of like being on a chain gang with your ball and chain.

00:16:52.779 --> 00:16:59.779
You know, sometimes our job gets in the way, but we always work it out.

00:16:59.779 --> 00:17:05.339
Except when we don't.

00:17:05.339 --> 00:17:12.380
Didn't I read an engagement announcement in The Daily Planet?

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:16.220
I thought we weren't going to bring that up, dear.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:20.269
Loss and I got her signals crossed.

00:17:20.269 --> 00:17:26.220
Yeah, I don't know how that I do slipped out.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:31.220
We're having so much fun, we're just enjoying taking it slowly now.

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:33.220
Well, you don't hear that very often.

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:36.220
I think it's nice to be a little old-fashioned.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:40.779
Well, yeah, people are in such a hurry these days.

00:17:40.779 --> 00:17:42.779
How's it working out for you, Lois?

00:17:42.779 --> 00:17:55.660
Well, um, Mrs. Kay, I can't keep blowing to you.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:18:02.420
Clark and I aren't really.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.500
working together at the Daily Planet. We were fired.

00:18:06.259 --> 00:18:08.819
And we aren't taking it slow. We're actually taking a break.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:18.579
The truth is, Clark, I need to find a way to make a difference with my life.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:28.190
And I realize now that I can't look to you or, or even the blur to make that happen for me.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:41.170
I need to do it on my own. So maybe what we need right now, isn't a break. It's a break up.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:58.700
Lois?

00:19:01.019 --> 00:19:03.019
Don't do this.

00:19:03.019 --> 00:19:09.299
If you care about me, then let me go.

00:19:09.299 --> 00:19:23.170
I'll see that she gets back today.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:26.170
I got a story that's just come up anyway.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.170
Here, let me help you.

00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:40.410
Thanks for dinner.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:41.410
My Clark.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:20:02.309
Are you okay?

00:20:02.309 --> 00:20:04.309
That'd be great.

00:20:04.309 --> 00:20:08.970
Zad, he burned you.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.970
We have to get out of here.

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:12.970
We have to get out of here.

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:13.970
Did this guy tell you what he wants?

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:14.970
I don't tell you what he wants.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:16.970
Said something about someone named the Red Queen and Gold,

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:19.970
Red Queen and Gold Diss, a bunch of aliens.

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:20.970
Really great stuff.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:21.970
Sunned right up your alley.

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:29.180
This whole thing's an act, right?

